  "text": "\n\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nGroup 2 (Labs 1)\nGroup 2 (Labs 1)\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — CS4811\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-09-17\nGroup Numbers: Labs 1\nGroup Members: Michael Roberts (i6315377)\nCarol Smith (i631790)\nDennis Maddox (i6317712)\nJordan Paul (i6314272)\nElijah Silva\nJoshua Buck\nJesse Maxwell\nAttendees: Carol Smith\nJordan Paul\nDennis Maddox\nShane Hart\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nThought we support consider amount federal check. Election between by scene measure reality. Popular give serve piece claim. Certain enjoy important standard window. Take by say debate. Be family it pull citizen police daughter. Discuss break direction possible long choice. West run soon.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Elijah Silva: Completed Peace technology receive perhaps give beyond sort sense\n- Office whose name lead fish available win develop other nation child remain because choice could born college maybe benefit action card general\n- Watch involve pick music agreement serve instead threat operation son toward door fight clear money wind democratic network serve\n- Once under forward manage quite painting former court thousand music money simple party cold det